# Catalogues are built on Windows and the server runs on Linux, so line endings
# are not left to whoever happens to commit. A shell script that reaches the
# server with CRLF fails as "bad interpreter" -- an error that names the
# interpreter, not the line endings, and reads like a missing binary.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.7z binary
*.data binary
*.wasm binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
